1
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:18,100
For over 30 years,
a man claiming

2
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:21,500
to be a descendant
of the Rockefellers

3
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:24,200
roamed the American elite circles.

4
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:26,700
He played the role
of an aristocrat

5
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:30,700
and exploited the social naivety
of the upper class,

6
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:33,700
who are easily dazzled
by a famous name.

7
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:37,900
This man, with his suits
and luxury art collection,

8
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:41,000
introduced himself
as Clark Rockefeller.

9
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Hardly anyone suspected him

10
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,000
until he was dragged
into criminal cases,

11
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,600
one of which targeted
his own biological daughter.

12
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:52,700
His lies were finally
and slowly uncovered.

13
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:56,400
The question is,
who exactly was Clark Rockefeller?

14
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:59,900
How could he deceive
the aristocrats for decades?

15
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:04,700
With Kamar Film, let's understand
who Clark Rockefeller really was.

16
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:06,600
Before the public knew him

17
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:09,100
as the eccentric
Clark Rockefeller,

18
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:10,800
the man began his life

19
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:13,200
as Christian Karl Gerhartsreiter,

20
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:15,100
born on February 21, 1961,

21
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:18,100
in a small town in Bavaria,
West Germany.

22
00:01:18,100 --> 00:01:21,200
He grew up in a simple
working-class family

23
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:23,200
as the son of a tailor

24
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:24,700
and a sawmill worker.

25
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:27,000
However, from his teenage years,

26
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,800
Christian had already shown
a rejection

27
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:31,800
of his fate as someone born

28
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:33,600
into an ordinary family.

29
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:36,400
An obsession with
American pop culture

30
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:38,800
and a dream to live in luxury

31
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:42,100
eventually pushed Christian
to leave Germany

32
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:44,800
in 1978, when he had
just turned 17,

33
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,500
using a tourist visa.

34
00:01:46,700 --> 00:01:49,500
For young Christian,
the United States

35
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:52,500
was not just a destination
or a new home,

36
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:56,000
but a grand stage
to begin his charade.

37
00:01:56,600 --> 00:01:59,700
Christian understood
that his true identity

38
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:02,800
as an immigrant
without wealth connections,

39
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,600
or valid legal documents

40
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:06,300
had to be buried deep

41
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:08,700
if he didn't want to be placed

42
00:02:08,700 --> 00:02:12,100
at the bottom
of the American social hierarchy.

43
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:14,600
So he began crafting
a new identity

44
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:16,700
as a successful person

45
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:19,300
so that people would believe him.

46
00:02:19,400 --> 00:02:22,200
Christian erased the traces
of his past

47
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:24,300
and rewrote his identity

48
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:27,100
as a figure
who could be well-received

49
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:29,200
by the American upper class.

50
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:31,900
This process
of changing identities

51
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:33,700
did not happen overnight,

52
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:36,500
but through a series
of identity shifts

53
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:39,200
that he designed
quite systematically

54
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:40,600
to avoid suspicion.

55
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:42,300
As his first experiment

56
00:02:42,300 --> 00:02:44,600
with a fake identity
in America,

57
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:48,500
Christian borrowed the name
of a 17th-century Puritan,

58
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:50,800
fanatic, and British politician.

59
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:54,100
Using an eccentric
and flamboyant personality,

60
00:02:54,100 --> 00:02:57,000
Christian arrived
in Connecticut in 1978

61
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,700
under the name
Christopher Chichester

62
00:02:59,700 --> 00:03:02,700
and successfully persuaded
a local family,

63
00:03:02,700 --> 00:03:04,700
the Savios, to take him in.

64
00:03:04,700 --> 00:03:08,200
He claimed to be
an independent exchange student

65
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:10,000
from Germany who was lost

66
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,700
and in need
of a place to stay.

67
00:03:12,700 --> 00:03:16,200
In the Savio home,
he began practicing his talent

68
00:03:16,200 --> 00:03:19,200
by pretending to be
a wealthy aristocrat,

69
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:22,200
saying his family owned yachts
in Europe,

70
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:25,000
and even demanding
the Savios treat him

71
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:28,100
with special status,
like a guest of honor.

72
00:03:28,100 --> 00:03:30,600
During his stay
at the Savio home,

73
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:32,800
he refused to do any housework

74
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:35,200
and acted as if
he were entitled

75
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:37,800
to be served by the family.

76
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:40,500
His arrogance
as an aristocrat

77
00:03:40,500 --> 00:03:42,300
became one of the reasons

78
00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:45,400
Christian was politely asked
to leave

79
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:46,900
by the Savio family.

80
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,600
Additionally, the Savio family
began

81
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:51,900
to grow suspicious
of his lies,

82
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:55,200
which were becoming
increasingly nonsensical.

83
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:58,200
After being expelled
from the Savio family

84
00:03:58,200 --> 00:04:01,400
in mid-1981, his identity
as his early alias

85
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:03,900
was buried, and Christian
continued

86
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:07,500
his adventurous charade
in San Marino, California,

87
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:09,000
using a new identity

88
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,800
as Christopher Mountbatten Chichester.

89
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:15,500
This time, Christian,
who was already 20 years old,

90
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:17,600
entered an elite neighborhood

91
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:21,100
filled with luxurious
Mediterranean-style homes.

92
00:04:21,100 --> 00:04:23,100
He crafted a fake backstory

93
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:24,800
as a British aristocrat

94
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:27,200
with the title
of Baronet or Sir,

95
00:04:27,200 --> 00:04:30,700
and Christian even claimed
to have direct kinship

96
00:04:30,700 --> 00:04:34,400
with Lord Mountbatten
and the British royal family.

97
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:38,200
To penetrate the very private
old-money social circle

98
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:40,600
in San Marino,
Christian launched

99
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:42,700
a meticulously planned scheme

100
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:45,400
to be seen as part
of the elite.

101
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:47,300
He always appeared dapper,

102
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:49,400
wearing gold-buttoned blazers

103
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:52,200
in the style
of elite Oxford students.

104
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:54,100
He carried a walking stick

105
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:56,500
and drove a classic Austin-Healey

106
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:59,900
or sometimes an old green
British pickup truck.

107
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:02,300
Additionally, Christian was known

108
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:04,300
to join the San Marino Club

109
00:05:04,300 --> 00:05:06,100
and was active in worship

110
00:05:06,100 --> 00:05:08,200
at the Church of Our Saviour.

111
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:10,700
With his intellectual-looking charm

112
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:13,000
and manufactured British accent,

113
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:14,900
the locals easily believed

114
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:16,700
his aristocratic status.

115
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:19,400
Not only that,
Christian even managed

116
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:22,900
to persuade the local community
cable TV station

117
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:25,600
to let him host
a talk show program

118
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:27,800
themed around art and culture.

119
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:30,700
This position gave him
a visual platform

120
00:05:30,700 --> 00:05:33,500
that further solidified
his reputation

121
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:35,500
in the eyes of the locals.

122
00:05:35,500 --> 00:05:39,300
Then, to complete his educated
aristocratic profile,

123
00:05:39,300 --> 00:05:41,900
Christian also focused
his ambitions

124
00:05:41,900 --> 00:05:45,300
on the University
of Southern California (USC),

125
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:49,100
one of the most prestigious campuses
in Los Angeles.

126
00:05:49,100 --> 00:05:50,500
He enrolled at USC

127
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:53,000
in the film or cinema arts program

128
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,700
using his fake identity

129
00:05:54,700 --> 00:05:56,600
as Christopher Chichester.

130
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:59,600
To bypass strict
administrative procedures

131
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:01,500
and document verification,

132
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:04,000
Christian forged
academic documents

133
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:07,500
claiming he had completed
his secondary education

134
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:09,800
at elite European institutions.

135
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:12,100
When asked
about legal documents

136
00:06:12,100 --> 00:06:15,900
like a foreign passport
or an official student visa,

137
00:06:15,900 --> 00:06:18,700
he used his diplomatic
or royal status

138
00:06:18,700 --> 00:06:21,200
and family connections
as an excuse

139
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:24,100
to avoid needing
standard documentation.

140
00:06:24,100 --> 00:06:26,200
While at USC, Christian acted

141
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:28,200
like a genius young director

142
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:30,800
who, once again,
appeared eccentric.

143
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:33,700
He was often seen
carrying film scripts,

144
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:36,800
discussing classic
European cinematography,

145
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:40,300
and mingling with students
from wealthy families.

146
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:43,700
However, he never finished
this academic career

147
00:06:43,700 --> 00:06:46,800
because his main focus
was never a diploma,

148
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:49,600
but rather using
his USC student status

149
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:53,000
as a social identity
to strengthen his position

150
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:54,000
in San Marino.

151
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,800
In 1982, it was recorded

152
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:58,300
that Christian rented
a guest house

153
00:06:58,300 --> 00:07:00,500
behind the home
of Didi Sohus,

154
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:02,700
a wealthy widow
with a history

155
00:07:02,700 --> 00:07:04,300
of alcohol dependency.

156
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:06,400
Didi lived with
her only son,

157
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:09,000
John Sohus,
and her daughter-in-law,

158
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:09,900
Linda Sohus.

159
00:07:09,900 --> 00:07:13,200
During his time living
with the Sohus family,

160
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:16,600
he exploited Didi's fragile
psychological state

161
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:20,000
by acting as her primary
protector and advisor,

162
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,900
which slowly caused a rift

163
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:24,200
between Didi and her own child.

164
00:07:24,200 --> 00:07:27,700
Meanwhile, John, who was gentle
and somewhat shy,

165
00:07:27,700 --> 00:07:30,100
and his wife,
who loved the arts,

166
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:31,800
initially had no issues

167
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:35,100
with the closeness
between Christian and Didi.

168
00:07:35,100 --> 00:07:37,000
Instead, they saw Kristian

169
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,500
as a unique
and influential person.

170
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:41,900
The married couple respected him.

171
00:07:41,900 --> 00:07:45,200
Especially since Kristian
often promised them

172
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:47,300
career assistance by claiming

173
00:07:47,300 --> 00:07:49,700
he had connections
to top circles

174
00:07:49,700 --> 00:07:53,000
in government
or the Hollywood film industry.

175
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:56,200
But then John and Linda
suddenly disappeared

176
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:57,200
in early 1985.

177
00:07:57,200 --> 00:08:00,000
Previously, Kristian
had told residents

178
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:02,200
that the couple went to Europe

179
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:03,700
for a secret mission

180
00:08:03,700 --> 00:08:06,500
arranged by his
diplomatic connections.

181
00:08:06,500 --> 00:08:09,700
Strangely, after John and Linda
disappeared,

182
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:12,300
Kristian actually
appeared panicked.

183
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:14,700
He hastily packed
his belongings,

184
00:08:14,700 --> 00:08:16,700
and also sold
or threw away

185
00:08:16,700 --> 00:08:18,500
his remaining furniture.

186
00:08:18,500 --> 00:08:22,000
Without saying goodbye,
Kristian fled San Marino

187
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:22,800
in mid-1985

188
00:08:22,800 --> 00:08:24,500
and buried his identity

189
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:26,400
as Christopher Chichester.

190
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:28,200
When he left San Marino,

191
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:31,000
he took John Sohus's
Honda pickup truck

192
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:33,300
with him toward the east coast.

193
00:08:33,300 --> 00:08:36,800
Kristian then appeared
in Greenwich, Connecticut,

194
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:38,600
an elite residential area

195
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:40,900
where investment bankers gather.

196
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:43,800
Here he used the name
Christopher Crowe.

197
00:08:43,800 --> 00:08:45,500
To survive in Greenwich

198
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:48,000
and penetrate
the corporate system

199
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,800
without a passport
or valid documents,

200
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:52,500
he stole and then used

201
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:55,000
the social security number,
or SSN,

202
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,000
of a man from Nebraska
named David Evans,

203
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,700
a civilian who was
completely unaware

204
00:09:00,700 --> 00:09:02,700
his identity was being used.

205
00:09:02,700 --> 00:09:04,500
Relying on the stolen SSN

206
00:09:04,500 --> 00:09:06,400
and a fake resume claiming

207
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:09,100
he was a graduate
of Yale University,

208
00:09:09,100 --> 00:09:12,400
it turned out Kristian
successfully penetrated

209
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:15,700
the heart of the Manhattan
financial industry

210
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:18,800
without ever having
formal higher education

211
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:21,200
or an official financial license.

212
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:24,900
Kristian only utilized
his self-taught intelligence

213
00:09:24,900 --> 00:09:26,900
and convincing body language

214
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:28,300
to lure recruiters.

215
00:09:28,300 --> 00:09:30,300
He then managed
to get hired

216
00:09:30,300 --> 00:09:33,200
at top-tier Wall Street
brokerage firms,

217
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:35,600
including Kidder, Peabody & [Co.]

218
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:37,100
And Nikko Securities.

219
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:40,100
In a short time, Kristian
was also trusted

220
00:09:40,100 --> 00:09:42,400
to manage investment portfolios

221
00:09:42,400 --> 00:09:44,300
worth millions of dollars.

222
00:09:44,300 --> 00:09:46,600
And he held
strategic positions

223
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:49,100
as a bond manager
and head analyst

224
00:09:49,100 --> 00:09:52,000
for capital market
investment decisions.

225
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:56,000
With this new life,
to support his Wall Street identity,

226
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,500
Kristian's lies grew
as he claimed

227
00:09:58,500 --> 00:10:01,400
to be a producer
for the television show

228
00:10:01,400 --> 00:10:02,800
Saturday Night Live

229
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:05,300
and the creator
of the initial idea

230
00:10:05,300 --> 00:10:07,400
for the hit film
The Goonies.

231
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:10,700
It seemed Kristian
was finally living the life

232
00:10:10,700 --> 00:10:12,200
he had long desired.

233
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:14,400
At that time,
he already lived

234
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:16,000
in a luxury apartment,

235
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:18,300
frequently consumed rare wines,

236
00:10:18,300 --> 00:10:20,000
and his image was known

237
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,700
as an eccentric genius.

238
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:24,900
Unfortunately, this life
built on falsehoods

239
00:10:24,900 --> 00:10:26,700
began to collapse in 1988

240
00:10:26,700 --> 00:10:28,700
when Kristian tried to sell

241
00:10:28,700 --> 00:10:30,500
John Sohus's pickup truck

242
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:32,900
to a local resident
in Greenwich.

243
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:34,800
Police found discrepancies

244
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:37,500
in the vehicle's
ownership documents,

245
00:10:37,500 --> 00:10:39,700
and detectives from California

246
00:10:39,700 --> 00:10:42,000
began tracking his whereabouts.

247
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:45,400
Kristian realized
that the police investigation

248
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:47,400
was closing in and his name

249
00:10:47,400 --> 00:10:49,200
was starting to be linked

250
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:52,200
to the disappearance
of the Sohus couple.

251
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:54,500
That is why
he suddenly resigned

252
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:57,200
from his position
at Nikko Securities

253
00:10:57,200 --> 00:10:57,900
in 1989.

254
00:10:57,900 --> 00:11:00,100
After that, Kristian was known

255
00:11:00,100 --> 00:11:02,700
to have cut off
all social contacts,

256
00:11:02,700 --> 00:11:04,600
erased his banking trails,

257
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:06,600
and wiped away the identity

258
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:08,100
of Christopher Crowe.

259
00:11:08,100 --> 00:11:10,100
Only then did Kristian reach

260
00:11:10,100 --> 00:11:12,000
the peak of his deception.

261
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,300
In the early 1990s
in Manhattan,

262
00:11:14,300 --> 00:11:16,600
he adopted
the most sacred name

263
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:19,000
in the American social hierarchy:

264
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:20,300
Clark Rockefeller.

265
00:11:20,300 --> 00:11:22,300
Christian didn't just claim

266
00:11:22,300 --> 00:11:24,600
to be an ordinary family member;

267
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:26,600
he crafted a specific story

268
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:28,300
that he was an heir

269
00:11:28,300 --> 00:11:31,700
to a European branch
of the Rockefeller dynasty

270
00:11:31,700 --> 00:11:34,500
that had intentionally
isolated itself,

271
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:37,300
often known
as the "lost Rockefeller."

272
00:11:37,300 --> 00:11:40,500
To cover the lack
of formal legal documents,

273
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:42,800
Christian created
a cunning lie

274
00:11:42,800 --> 00:11:44,200
to protect himself,

275
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:46,500
claiming he had no ID,
passport,

276
00:11:46,500 --> 00:11:48,900
driver's license,
or bank account

277
00:11:48,900 --> 00:11:51,600
for the sake
of his family's security

278
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:53,500
against kidnapping threats

279
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:56,300
and the dynasty's
secret belief system.

280
00:11:56,300 --> 00:11:59,400
He even claimed
his entire financial assets

281
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:03,200
were managed by a trust fund—
a family entity abroad

282
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:05,000
that only dealt in cash,

283
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,800
which miraculously worked

284
00:12:06,800 --> 00:12:09,200
within the New York
elite circles

285
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:10,200
at the time.

286
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:12,400
This strange and absurd reason

287
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:14,100
wasn't seen as a lie,

288
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:16,100
but swallowed whole as part

289
00:12:16,100 --> 00:12:18,100
of an "Old Money" lifestyle.

290
00:12:18,100 --> 00:12:20,600
Using the Rockefeller name
provided

291
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:23,100
an instant psychological advantage,

292
00:12:23,100 --> 00:12:26,000
and Christian seemed
well aware of this.

293
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:30,000
Within elite circles,
questioning the proof of identity

294
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:31,700
or financial background

295
00:12:31,700 --> 00:12:34,500
of someone claiming
to be a Rockefeller

296
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:35,900
was considered rude

297
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:38,300
and a breach
of social etiquette.

298
00:12:38,300 --> 00:12:40,300
No one dared to doubt him,

299
00:12:40,300 --> 00:12:42,200
let alone verify his data,

300
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:44,300
when it concerned an identity

301
00:12:44,300 --> 00:12:47,600
whose power and wealth
were seen as limitless.

302
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:50,700
In 1993, Christian's trail
of life and lies

303
00:12:50,700 --> 00:12:52,000
went even further.

304
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:55,300
He attended a Quaker-themed party
in New York

305
00:12:55,300 --> 00:12:56,800
and met Sandra Boss,

306
00:12:56,800 --> 00:13:00,500
a young genius
and Harvard Business School graduate

307
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:03,300
who would later become
a senior partner

308
00:13:03,300 --> 00:13:07,000
at the renowned consulting firm
McKinsey & Company.

309
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:10,300
Sandra, captivated
by his intellectual style,

310
00:13:10,300 --> 00:13:12,300
knowledge of high-value art,

311
00:13:12,300 --> 00:13:14,000
and Rockefeller status,

312
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:16,700
eventually married Christian
in 1995.

313
00:13:16,700 --> 00:13:18,900
During their 12-year marriage,

314
00:13:18,900 --> 00:13:21,700
Sandra became
the sole financial pillar

315
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:25,000
of the family,
funding their lavish lifestyle,

316
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:28,000
including the purchase
of a historic home

317
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:29,900
in Cornish, New Hampshire,

318
00:13:29,900 --> 00:13:31,900
and a luxury home in Boston.

319
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:35,000
Meanwhile, Christian spent
his wife's money

320
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,100
on expensive art,
memberships

321
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:40,100
at the exclusive Algonquin Club
in Boston,

322
00:13:40,100 --> 00:13:43,500
and psychologically controlled
her private life

323
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:46,000
through manipulation
and isolation.

324
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:49,000
Their relationship culminated
in the birth

325
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:52,700
of their daughter,
named Reigh Storrow Rockefeller,

326
00:13:52,700 --> 00:13:55,200
who was nicknamed "Snooks"
in 2001.

327
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:57,900
It was the presence
of their daughter

328
00:13:57,900 --> 00:14:00,300
that finally opened Sandra's eyes

329
00:14:00,300 --> 00:14:02,200
to her husband's oddities.

330
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:05,800
From Christian's inability
to hold legal documents

331
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:07,400
in their child's name,

332
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:09,100
his fear of the police,

333
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:11,900
to his increasingly
paranoid behavior.

334
00:14:11,900 --> 00:14:14,300
Feeling uneasy
about her husband,

335
00:14:14,300 --> 00:14:16,800
Sandra hired
a private investigator

336
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:18,800
to file for divorce in 2007,

337
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:22,600
and that independent investigation
finally uncovered

338
00:14:22,600 --> 00:14:26,800
that her husband's
social security number was unregistered

339
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:30,000
and the name Clark Rockefeller
did not exist

340
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,900
in the official Rockefeller
family tree.

341
00:14:32,900 --> 00:14:36,000
This fact allowed Sandra
to win her divorce

342
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,900
and gain full custody
of their daughter.

343
00:14:38,900 --> 00:14:42,900
But ironically, Christian
then took desperate measures.

344
00:14:42,900 --> 00:14:45,900
He kidnapped his own daughter
in July 2008

345
00:14:45,900 --> 00:14:49,400
in Boston during
a supervised visitation session

346
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:50,900
with a social worker.

347
00:14:50,900 --> 00:14:53,200
It is known that Kristian
pushed

348
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:55,200
the supervisor to the ground

349
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:58,000
and fled with his
7-year-old daughter.

350
00:14:58,000 --> 00:14:59,700
They got into an SUV

351
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:01,500
driven by a hired driver.

352
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:03,500
With a large amount of cash

353
00:15:03,500 --> 00:15:06,900
he had prepared,
Kristian escaped to Baltimore.

354
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:09,400
There, he used
a new fake identity

355
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:10,900
as Charles Chip Smith

356
00:15:10,900 --> 00:15:13,600
and bought a house
with a boat dock

357
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:16,400
because he planned
to sail his daughter

358
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:18,400
out of [U.S.] Jurisdiction.

359
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:21,300
This desperate act
by Kristian triggered

360
00:15:21,300 --> 00:15:24,300
an emergency nationwide manhunt
by the FBI

361
00:15:24,300 --> 00:15:27,800
through phone signal tracking,
cash transactions,

362
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:30,400
and reports from
a real estate agent

363
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:31,700
in East Baltimore

364
00:15:31,700 --> 00:15:34,100
who grew suspicious
of the buyer.

365
00:15:34,100 --> 00:15:35,900
Where Kristian was hiding

366
00:15:35,900 --> 00:15:38,900
was finally successfully
mapped by the FBI

367
00:15:38,900 --> 00:15:40,300
in just 6 days.

368
00:15:40,300 --> 00:15:41,700
On August 2, 2008,

369
00:15:41,700 --> 00:15:43,500
FBI agents devised a trap

370
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:45,700
by pretending
to tell Kristian

371
00:15:45,700 --> 00:15:47,700
that his yacht was leaking.

372
00:15:47,700 --> 00:15:50,200
When Kristian came out
of the house

373
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:51,600
to check the boat,

374
00:15:51,600 --> 00:15:54,900
the FBI SWAT team
immediately apprehended him

375
00:15:54,900 --> 00:15:56,300
without resistance.

376
00:15:56,300 --> 00:15:58,600
His daughter
was finally rescued

377
00:15:58,600 --> 00:16:00,400
without a single injury.

378
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:01,700
After his arrest,

379
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:05,800
Kristian's fingerprints,
matched to a case in San Marino,

380
00:16:05,800 --> 00:16:08,300
immediately exposed
the dark events

381
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:10,700
hidden behind
his luxurious life.

382
00:16:10,700 --> 00:16:12,700
In May 1994, the new owner

383
00:16:12,700 --> 00:16:15,000
of the former Sohus family home

384
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:16,700
in the San Marino area

385
00:16:16,700 --> 00:16:19,000
decided to build
a swimming pool

386
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,200
in the backyard.

387
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:22,700
When heavy equipment
began digging

388
00:16:22,700 --> 00:16:25,000
the ground
near the guest house

389
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:26,900
once occupied by Kristian,

390
00:16:26,900 --> 00:16:29,200
the machine hit
a solid object.

391
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:31,300
Several feet deep,
they found

392
00:16:31,300 --> 00:16:33,500
three thick plastic trash bags

393
00:16:33,500 --> 00:16:34,500
buried neatly.

394
00:16:34,500 --> 00:16:38,000
Surprisingly, inside were
human skeletal remains

395
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,300
along with remnants
of clothing

396
00:16:40,300 --> 00:16:42,000
and two fiberglass bags

397
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:45,700
bearing the University
of Southern California logo.

398
00:16:45,700 --> 00:16:47,500
Forensic tests confirmed

399
00:16:47,500 --> 00:16:50,500
that the remains
were those of John Sohus,

400
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:52,800
who died from
blunt force trauma

401
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:53,800
to the head.

402
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:57,400
However, the whereabouts
of his wife, Linda Sohus,

403
00:16:57,400 --> 00:16:58,700
were never found,

404
00:16:58,700 --> 00:17:01,000
remaining a mystery
to this day.

405
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:02,400
For over a decade,

406
00:17:02,400 --> 00:17:05,600
San Marino police held
the Sohus murder case

407
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:07,500
without a definite suspect

408
00:17:07,500 --> 00:17:09,800
because Christopher Chichester,

409
00:17:09,800 --> 00:17:11,800
linked to the Sohus family,

410
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:13,100
suddenly vanished

411
00:17:13,100 --> 00:17:16,100
without leaving
any formal documentation.

412
00:17:16,100 --> 00:17:18,500
The key to the case
only opened

413
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:21,200
after Kristian's arrest
in Baltimore,

414
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:24,700
where his fingerprints
connected him to the case.

415
00:17:24,700 --> 00:17:27,200
Furthermore,
immigration databases

416
00:17:27,200 --> 00:17:30,200
then completely revealed
his true identity

417
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:33,500
as Christian Karl Gerhartsreiter
from Germany.

418
00:17:33,500 --> 00:17:35,000
These existing proofs

419
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:38,000
not only uncovered
a series of fraud cases

420
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:41,000
but also became
a first-degree murder case

421
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:42,600
committed by Kristian.

422
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:44,500
Kristian had to face trial

423
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:47,600
and multiple sentences
for child abduction.

424
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:50,500
The inaugural trial
was held in mid-2009

425
00:17:50,500 --> 00:17:53,300
at the Suffolk Superior Court,
Boston.

426
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:55,600
And this became
the first moment

427
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:58,100
when his true identity
was exposed

428
00:17:58,100 --> 00:17:59,600
openly to the public.

429
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:02,400
During the trial,
Kristian's legal team

430
00:18:02,400 --> 00:18:05,200
employed an insanity
defense strategy.

431
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:08,900
The lawyers brought in
a psychiatric expert witness

432
00:18:08,900 --> 00:18:11,400
who stated that Christian suffered

433
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:13,900
from a severe
personality disorder

434
00:18:13,900 --> 00:18:16,700
and narcissistic
personality disorder.

435
00:18:16,700 --> 00:18:18,500
According to the defense,

436
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:21,300
Christian truly believed
all this time

437
00:18:21,300 --> 00:18:23,200
that he was a Rockefeller,

438
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:26,000
and his act of kidnapping
his daughter

439
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,400
was driven by
a delusional belief

440
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:30,500
that his child was in danger.

441
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:33,800
However, the prosecution
refuted these claims

442
00:18:33,800 --> 00:18:36,600
by showing just how
calculated and cold

443
00:18:36,600 --> 00:18:37,900
his actions were.

444
00:18:37,900 --> 00:18:40,900
He had even hired a driver
well in advance

445
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:43,400
and purchased
a waterfront property

446
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:45,100
in Baltimore with cash.

447
00:18:45,100 --> 00:18:48,300
Christian also neatly concealed
his identity

448
00:18:48,300 --> 00:18:50,300
and the trail of his escape

449
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:52,900
from the pursuit
of the authorities.

450
00:18:52,900 --> 00:18:55,100
His meticulous planning proved

451
00:18:55,100 --> 00:18:57,300
that Christian was fully aware

452
00:18:57,300 --> 00:19:00,300
of the illegal actions
he was committing.

453
00:19:00,300 --> 00:19:02,800
Defeated in arguments
and evidence,

454
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:04,200
on June 12, 2009,

455
00:19:04,200 --> 00:19:07,000
the jury finally found
Christian guilty

456
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:09,500
of parental kidnapping
and assault

457
00:19:09,500 --> 00:19:11,000
with a deadly weapon

458
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:14,300
related to his act of shoving
a social worker,

459
00:19:14,300 --> 00:19:16,700
causing injury
during his escape.

460
00:19:16,700 --> 00:19:18,400
The judge sentenced him

461
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:20,100
to 4 to 5 years

462
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:23,100
in a Massachusetts
correctional facility.

463
00:19:23,100 --> 00:19:26,100
While Christian was serving
this sentence,

464
00:19:26,100 --> 00:19:29,500
the Rockefeller identity
he had previously used

465
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:30,800
was legally erased

466
00:19:30,800 --> 00:19:33,200
and his name
in the prison system

467
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:35,400
was restored
to his real name.

468
00:19:35,400 --> 00:19:38,100
While Christian was serving
his time,

469
00:19:38,100 --> 00:19:39,600
the San Marino police

470
00:19:39,600 --> 00:19:43,400
and the Los Angeles County
District Attorney's Office

471
00:19:43,400 --> 00:19:46,700
were busy building
much more serious charges.

472
00:19:46,700 --> 00:19:49,500
Once he reached the end
of his sentence

473
00:19:49,500 --> 00:19:51,300
in Massachusetts in 2011,

474
00:19:51,300 --> 00:19:54,900
Christian was immediately
extradited to California

475
00:19:54,900 --> 00:19:57,700
to face charges
of first-degree murder

476
00:19:57,700 --> 00:19:58,700
of John Sohus.

477
00:19:58,700 --> 00:20:00,500
The murder trial was held

478
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:01,500
in early 2013

479
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:03,500
and proceeded very fiercely.

480
00:20:03,500 --> 00:20:06,300
His legal team tried
to shift the blame

481
00:20:06,300 --> 00:20:09,400
onto Linda Sohus,
who has never been found,

482
00:20:09,400 --> 00:20:12,400
by claiming that Linda
killed her husband

483
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:13,400
and then fled.

484
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:16,300
Meanwhile, Christian
was merely a victim

485
00:20:16,300 --> 00:20:19,800
of circumstance
who happened to be at the scene.

486
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:23,500
However, the prosecutor
presented physical evidence

487
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:25,300
that could not be denied.

488
00:20:25,300 --> 00:20:27,500
This included a fiberglass bag

489
00:20:27,500 --> 00:20:30,800
with a University
of Southern California logo

490
00:20:30,800 --> 00:20:33,300
that wrapped John Sohus's remains.

491
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:34,700
Where in the 1980s,

492
00:20:34,700 --> 00:20:36,800
Christian was the only person

493
00:20:36,800 --> 00:20:40,100
in that neighborhood
who was enrolled at USC.

494
00:20:40,100 --> 00:20:43,900
Furthermore, Christian's act
of selling John Sohus's

495
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:45,900
pickup truck in Connecticut

496
00:20:45,900 --> 00:20:48,500
shortly after the victim
disappeared

497
00:20:48,500 --> 00:20:51,500
became direct evidence
of his involvement

498
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:53,400
after a fairly long trial.

499
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:54,800
On April 10, 2013,

500
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:57,300
the Los Angeles Superior Court
jury

501
00:20:57,300 --> 00:21:00,600
found Christian guilty
of first-degree murder.

502
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:04,300
Four months later,
specifically on August 15, 2013,

503
00:21:04,300 --> 00:21:06,700
Judge Marcus Kuming
sentenced him

504
00:21:06,700 --> 00:21:09,100
to 27 years to life
in prison.

505
00:21:09,100 --> 00:21:12,600
The judge emphasized
that Christian demonstrated

506
00:21:12,600 --> 00:21:15,100
sociopathic,
manipulative behavior

507
00:21:15,100 --> 00:21:17,900
and never showed
the slightest remorse

508
00:21:17,900 --> 00:21:19,900
for the life
he had taken.

509
00:21:19,900 --> 00:21:22,400
This sentence was added
separately

510
00:21:22,400 --> 00:21:24,400
from the kidnapping sentence

511
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:25,900
he served in Boston.

512
00:21:25,900 --> 00:21:29,000
Christian, who had spent
more than 30 years

513
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:31,300
pretending to be
an aristocrat,

514
00:21:31,300 --> 00:21:32,800
a Wall Street broker,

515
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:35,600
and an heir
to the Rockefeller dynasty,

516
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:38,000
must spend the rest
of his life

517
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:38,900
behind bars.

518
00:21:38,900 --> 00:21:40,900
There are no more
big names

519
00:21:40,900 --> 00:21:43,400
or fake statuses
that can save him.

520
00:21:43,400 --> 00:21:46,100
Today, Christian
is still languishing

521
00:21:46,100 --> 00:21:48,300
at the Mule Creek State Prison

522
00:21:48,300 --> 00:21:49,800
in Ione, California.

523
00:21:49,800 --> 00:21:52,900
A prison with
a medium-high security level.

524
00:21:52,900 --> 00:21:54,300
Now in his sixties,

525
00:21:54,300 --> 00:21:56,800
the man once accustomed
to luxury,

526
00:21:56,800 --> 00:21:59,700
aristocratic service,
and high-value art

527
00:21:59,700 --> 00:22:02,500
must now live
a uniform prison routine

528
00:22:02,500 --> 00:22:04,300
under his real identity.

529
00:22:04,300 --> 00:22:06,400
Based on his 2013 sentencing,

530
00:22:06,400 --> 00:22:08,400
the earliest he is eligible

531
00:22:08,400 --> 00:22:09,800
to apply for parole

532
00:22:09,800 --> 00:22:11,300
is in the mid-2030s.

533
00:22:11,300 --> 00:22:14,600
However, considering the nature
of his crimes

534
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:17,900
and his highly problematic
behavioral history,

535
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,600
legal observers believe

536
00:22:19,600 --> 00:22:22,100
there is little chance
for Kristian

537
00:22:22,100 --> 00:22:23,900
to ever walk free again.

538
00:22:23,900 --> 00:22:24,300
Yeah.
